  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Set cookies",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {\r",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
              "});\r",
              "\r",
              "pm.test(\"Cookies are returned in the response body\", function () {\r",
              "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();\r",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.cookies).to.have.property('foo1', 'bar1');\r",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.cookies).to.have.property('foo3', 'bar3');\r",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BaseUrl}}cookies/set?foo1=bar1&foo2=bar2\n&foo3=bar3&foo4=bar4",
          "host": [
            "{{BaseUrl}}cookies"
          ],
          "path": [
            "set"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "foo1",
              "value": "bar1"
            },
            {
              "key": "foo2",
              "value": "bar2\n"
            },
            {
              "key": "foo3",
              "value": "bar3"
            },
            {
              "key": "foo4",
              "value": "bar4"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get cookies",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Verify cookies are retrieved\", function () {\r",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
              "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();\r",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.cookies).to.not.be.empty;\r",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{BaseUrl}}cookies",
          "host": [
            "{{BaseUrl}}cookies"
          ]
        },
        "description": "## Get Cookies\n\nRetrieves all cookies currently associated with the request session.\n\nThis endpoint returns a JSON object containing all cookies sent with the request. It is useful for verifying that cookies have been correctly set in a prior request (e.g., via the `/cookies/set` endpoint).\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method:** GET\n- **URL:** `{{BaseUrl}}cookies`\n- **Auth:** None required\n- **Headers:** None required\n\n### Response\n\nReturns a `200 OK` with a JSON body containing a `cookies` object, where each key-value pair represents a cookie name and its value.\n\n**Example Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"cookies\": {\n    \"foo1\": \"bar1\",\n    \"foo2\": \"bar2\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- Use the `Set cookies` request first to populate cookies before calling this endpoint.\n- The `BaseUrl` variable should be set to `https://postman-echo.com/`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
